<title>INDIA: India's IDBI contracts $50.0 mln loan.</title>
<headline>India's IDBI contracts $50.0 mln loan.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Industrial Development Bank of India (IDBI) said it signed a $50 million seven-year loan arranged by Asahi Finance (Hong Kong) Ltd with The Asahi Bank Ltd, Hong Kong Branch, as the lender.</p>
<p>The loan which has on all-in-cost of 60 bps over LIBOR is the finest pricing achieved by an Indian borrower for a such maturity, IDBI said in a statement.</p>
<p>The loan from Asahi Bank will be utilised by IDBI for onlending to its clients for import of capital goods and for project related rupee expenditure, IDBI said.</p>
<p>IDBI is India's leading long-term lending bank.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
